      <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        This calendar tracks pole-vault competition opportunities outside the normal Arizona high-school and collegiate seasons. It is for coaches, athletes, and parents who want additional meets, from open all-comers events to youth championships, masters meets, national high-school meets, street and beach vaults, and elite qualifying competitions.
      </p>
      <p class="notice notice-info">
        <strong>Last researched September 28, 2026.</strong>
        Treat this as a living calendar. Any item marked Monitor stays date-free until a current organizer or governing-body page confirms the new edition. AZPVA travel packages, including the Reno Summit trip, are listed separately on <a href="/events">Events</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-to-read">How to read this calendar</h2>
      <div class="legend">
        <article class="legend-item">
          <span class="badge confirmed">Confirmed</span>
          <p>The organizer or governing body has published the 2027 date.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="legend-item">
          <span class="badge monitor">Monitor</span>
          <p>The event is established and recurring, but a 2027 date is not yet published.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="legend-item">
          <span class="badge qualifying">Qualifying</span>
          <p>Entry requires a performance standard, advancement pathway, invitation, or other eligibility requirement.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="legend-item">
          <span class="badge open-entry">Open</span>
          <p>Broad registration is available, subject to age, division, and capacity rules.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p>
        Audience labels such as Masters, High school, Youth, Elite, and Street vault describe who the meet serves. A gold left border on a card means the date is still Monitor. Prices, standards, and deadlines that are still labeled for a prior year are called out in the card and should not be copied forward.
      </p>

